# 🏗️ Step 1 — Fetch Nodes For Document Set

We need a SQL function:

### Input

* vault_id
* document_id list

### Output

* minimal flat node list
* only required nodes

---

## SQL: Fetch Contextual Subtree

```sql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION semantic_tree_v2.fetch_subtree_for_documents(
    p_user_id UUID,
    p_vault_id UUID,
    p_document_ids UUID[]
) RETURNS JSONB
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
DECLARE
    result JSONB;
BEGIN
    -- Permission check
    IF NOT semantic_tree_v2.user_has_vault_role(p_user_id, p_vault_id, 'viewer') THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'insufficient_privilege';
    END IF;

    WITH RECURSIVE doc_nodes AS (
        SELECT DISTINCT nd.node_id, nd.vault_id
        FROM semantic_tree_v2.node_document nd
        WHERE nd.vault_id = p_vault_id
          AND nd.document_id = ANY(p_document_ids)
    ),
    ancestors AS (
        SELECT tn.id, tn.parent_id, tn.vault_id, tn.title, tn.node_type
        FROM semantic_tree_v2.tree_node tn
        JOIN doc_nodes dn
          ON tn.id = dn.node_id

        UNION ALL

        SELECT parent.id, parent.parent_id, parent.vault_id, parent.title, parent.node_type
        FROM semantic_tree_v2.tree_node parent
        JOIN ancestors child
          ON child.parent_id = parent.id
         AND parent.vault_id = p_vault_id
    )
    SELECT jsonb_agg(DISTINCT jsonb_build_object(
        'id', id,
        'parent_id', parent_id,
        'title', title,
        'node_type', node_type
    ))
    INTO result
    FROM ancestors;

    RETURN COALESCE(result, '[]'::jsonb);
END $$;
```

This returns only:

* Nodes directly attached to documents
* Their ancestors up to root

No full tree download.

